{"duration_api_ms":273614,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"c338c711-e934-45b2-b285-4d217973fcf7","total_cost_usd":1.4887584000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":140,"cache_creation_input_tokens":74381,"cache_read_input_tokens":4597497,"output_tokens":26731,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3114},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":74381,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2847,"cache_read_input_tokens":91074,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4065,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004145,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":140,"outputTokens":26731,"cacheReadInputTokens":4597497,"cacheCreationInputTokens":74381,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4846134000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3114,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":112,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured a 3-node MariaDB 10.6 Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) on RHEL 7.9. Since RHEL 7 is EOL for the official MariaDB repo tooling and had no base OS repo configured, I manually pointed yum at the MariaDB archive (archive.mariadb.org, mariadb-10.6/rhel7-amd64) plus a CentOS 7 vault base repo (node3 only, for missing perl/libaio/boost deps), installed MariaDB-server + galera-4, opened firewalld ports 3306/4567/4568/4444, and wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and rsync-based SST. Bootstrapped node1 with galera_new_cluster, then started node2 and node3 which joined via SST, reaching a 3-node Synced/Primary cluster. Verified multi-master write propagation (writes from each of the 3 nodes visible on the others). Demonstrated availability during a member outage: stopped node3, confirmed the cluster stayed Primary at cluster_size=2, wrote a row via node1, restarted node3, and confirmed it automatically resynced (IST) back to Synced/cluster_size=3 with the row present. Then executed the mandatory node-restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id + wsrep health on all 3 nodes, restarted node1, node2, and node3 sequentially via `systemctl reboot` (one at a time, quorum preserved throughout — never below 2/3), polled each until exec was available again, confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed each node's mariadb.service was active and rejoined the cluster (Synced/Primary/size=3) before moving to the next. A final post-restart write/read check across all three nodes confirmed the cluster still works end-to-end. Root and SST credentials were generated on-node and only ever passed via secret_env in later commands (not left in final report).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Investigated OS (RHEL 7.9) and lack of any configured yum repos on all 3 nodes\",\"Configured MariaDB 10.6 archive yum repo (archive.mariadb.org/mariadb-10.6/yum/rhel7-amd64) with imported GPG key on node1, node2, node3\",\"Added CentOS 7 vault base repo on node3 to satisfy perl/libaio/boost-program-options dependencies missing from the base image\",\"Installed MariaDB-server, MariaDB-client, galera-4, rsync on all 3 nodes\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306/tcp, 4567/tcp+udp, 4568/tcp, 4444/tcp on all 3 nodes\",\"Appended CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all 3 nodes\",\"Generated SST and root passwords on node1 and wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and node-specific wsrep_node_address/name on all 3 nodes\",\"Bootstrapped Galera on node1 via galera_new_cluster; set root password and created sst_user via SQL\",\"Started mariadb on node2 and node3, confirmed both joined via SST reaching wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary\",\"Verified multi-master write propagation with inserts from node1, node2, node3 all visible cluster-wide\",\"Enabled mariadb.service on boot on all 3 nodes\",\"Captured healthy baseline (wsrep status + service active) on all 3 nodes before disruption\",\"Stopped mariadb on node3, verified cluster stayed Primary at size=2 and accepted a write via node1 that replicated to node2\",\"Restarted mariadb on node3, verified automatic IST resync back to size=3/Synced/Primary with the during-outage row present\",\"Captured baseline boot_id (kernel random boot_id) plus wsrep health on all 3 nodes for the restart protocol\",\"Sequentially rebooted node1, then node2, then node3 via `systemctl reboot` (backgrounded so the ack returned pre-disconnect), one at a time, preserving 2/3 quorum throughout\",\"Polled each node until exec access returned, confirmed changed boot_id proving an actual restart, and confirmed mariadb.service active + cluster rejoined (Synced/Primary/size=3) before restarting the next node\",\"Ran a final post-all-restarts write/read validation across all 3 nodes confirming continued multi-master replication\",\"Dropped test databases (galtest, finaltest) used for validation\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-member Galera cluster established; writes through any member visible from the others\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8ef98bab699d4e35\",\"cmd-09f76ca8cc1e47ee\",\"cmd-541585bd9d4f4bb0\",\"cmd-873107735c5e4144\",\"cmd-04b90b6794ce410b\",\"cmd-88d46dda715e48ec\",\"cmd-d0352da58d664ab7\",\"cmd-bc29bddd1d204c36\",\"cmd-d7216643cc8a4b2f\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped, node2/node3 joined reaching cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary; inserts made from node2, node1, and node3 were each visible on the other two members\"},{\"requirement\":\"Database stays available with one member down; that member auto-resyncs on return\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a8b1f00b424d4310\",\"cmd-1a81dc161d714053\",\"cmd-949aa62380b94f87\",\"cmd-fe09e7df052a4766\",\"cmd-0ecec26495294e8d\"],\"summary\":\"Stopped node3 (baseline Synced captured first); cluster remained Primary at size=2 and accepted/replicated a write via node1; node3 restarted and automatically resynced to size=3/Synced with the during-outage row present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered cluster state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-aa2a682e4153445d\",\"cmd-a30a0cbe486d4d35\",\"cmd-64e12e52369d4cfb\",\"cmd-dee67fe891e14c29\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d72bd4ec.../Synced captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; post-restart boot_id bf08c354... (changed); mariadb active and cluster size=3/Synced/Primary after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered cluster state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-89cc583add3d4395\",\"cmd-479ce26f6a604a9e\",\"cmd-4a92dfdf587d4b9f\",\"cmd-5d2cdd8d16834263\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 809708f3.../Synced captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; post-restart boot_id 537fec0c... (changed); mariadb active and cluster size=3/Synced/Primary after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered cluster state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6345555516ee4f91\",\"cmd-96937f57c21e467b\",\"cmd-c93acf25efaa4837\",\"cmd-3ea3a4d3e30846bb\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 73bafeef.../Synced captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; post-restart boot_id 27da3e81... (changed); mariadb active and cluster size=3/Synced/Primary, all 3 wsrep_incoming_addresses present after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"End-to-end functionality confirmed after all three sequential restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-03414e3a38554b1f\",\"cmd-a967339835df4fba\",\"cmd-dfa1a18c9b6e4412\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart write from node1 was visible on node2 and node3, and a subsequent write from node2 was visible on node3, confirming multi-master replication still functions after the full restart cycle\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a 3-node MariaDB 10.6 Galera cluster (node1, node2, node3) on RHEL 7.9. Since RHEL 7 is EOL for the official MariaDB repo tooling and had no base OS repo configured, I manually pointed yum at the MariaDB archive (archive.mariadb.org, mariadb-10.6/rhel7-amd64) plus a CentOS 7 vault base repo (node3 only, for missing perl/libaio/boost deps), installed MariaDB-server + galera-4, opened firewalld ports 3306/4567/4568/4444, and wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and rsync-based SST. Bootstrapped node1 with galera_new_cluster, then started node2 and node3 which joined via SST, reaching a 3-node Synced/Primary cluster. Verified multi-master write propagation (writes from each of the 3 nodes visible on the others). Demonstrated availability during a member outage: stopped node3, confirmed the cluster stayed Primary at cluster_size=2, wrote a row via node1, restarted node3, and confirmed it automatically resynced (IST) back to Synced/cluster_size=3 with the row present. Then executed the mandatory node-restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id + wsrep health on all 3 nodes, restarted node1, node2, and node3 sequentially via `systemctl reboot` (one at a time, quorum preserved throughout — never below 2/3), polled each until exec was available again, confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed each node's mariadb.service was active and rejoined the cluster (Synced/Primary/size=3) before moving to the next. A final post-restart write/read check across all three nodes confirmed the cluster still works end-to-end. Root and SST credentials were generated on-node and only ever passed via secret_env in later commands (not left in final report).","actions_performed":["Investigated OS (RHEL 7.9) and lack of any configured yum repos on all 3 nodes","Configured MariaDB 10.6 archive yum repo (archive.mariadb.org/mariadb-10.6/yum/rhel7-amd64) with imported GPG key on node1, node2, node3","Added CentOS 7 vault base repo on node3 to satisfy perl/libaio/boost-program-options dependencies missing from the base image","Installed MariaDB-server, MariaDB-client, galera-4, rsync on all 3 nodes","Opened firewalld ports 3306/tcp, 4567/tcp+udp, 4568/tcp, 4444/tcp on all 3 nodes","Appended CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all 3 nodes","Generated SST and root passwords on node1 and wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and node-specific wsrep_node_address/name on all 3 nodes","Bootstrapped Galera on node1 via galera_new_cluster; set root password and created sst_user via SQL","Started mariadb on node2 and node3, confirmed both joined via SST reaching wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary","Verified multi-master write propagation with inserts from node1, node2, node3 all visible cluster-wide","Enabled mariadb.service on boot on all 3 nodes","Captured healthy baseline (wsrep status + service active) on all 3 nodes before disruption","Stopped mariadb on node3, verified cluster stayed Primary at size=2 and accepted a write via node1 that replicated to node2","Restarted mariadb on node3, verified automatic IST resync back to size=3/Synced/Primary with the during-outage row present","Captured baseline boot_id (kernel random boot_id) plus wsrep health on all 3 nodes for the restart protocol","Sequentially rebooted node1, then node2, then node3 via `systemctl reboot` (backgrounded so the ack returned pre-disconnect), one at a time, preserving 2/3 quorum throughout","Polled each node until exec access returned, confirmed changed boot_id proving an actual restart, and confirmed mariadb.service active + cluster rejoined (Synced/Primary/size=3) before restarting the next node","Ran a final post-all-restarts write/read validation across all 3 nodes confirming continued multi-master replication","Dropped test databases (galtest, finaltest) used for validation"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-member Galera cluster established; writes through any member visible from the others","command_ids":["cmd-8ef98bab699d4e35","cmd-09f76ca8cc1e47ee","cmd-541585bd9d4f4bb0","cmd-873107735c5e4144","cmd-04b90b6794ce410b","cmd-88d46dda715e48ec","cmd-d0352da58d664ab7","cmd-bc29bddd1d204c36","cmd-d7216643cc8a4b2f"],"summary":"node1 bootstrapped, node2/node3 joined reaching cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary; inserts made from node2, node1, and node3 were each visible on the other two members"},{"requirement":"Database stays available with one member down; that member auto-resyncs on return","command_ids":["cmd-a8b1f00b424d4310","cmd-1a81dc161d714053","cmd-949aa62380b94f87","cmd-fe09e7df052a4766","cmd-0ecec26495294e8d"],"summary":"Stopped node3 (baseline Synced captured first); cluster remained Primary at size=2 and accepted/replicated a write via node1; node3 restarted and automatically resynced to size=3/Synced with the during-outage row present"},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered cluster state","command_ids":["cmd-aa2a682e4153445d","cmd-a30a0cbe486d4d35","cmd-64e12e52369d4cfb","cmd-dee67fe891e14c29"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id d72bd4ec.../Synced captured; systemctl reboot issued and acknowledged; post-restart boot_id bf08c354.